  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-02-16T01:00:59.287Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "After the latest client update, VRCContactReceiver components will always set the state of their driven parameter to zero/false when the local user triggers it, even when configured to only respond to other avatars.\n\n# Reproduction\n\n1. Create a toggle menu item for a boolean parameter to visualize this bug.\n\n2. Set up a VRCContactReceiver on the avatar. Target the same parameter as the menu item. Tick 'Allow Others' and 'Local Only'. Untick 'Allow Self'.\n\n3. Trigger this contact receiver yourself.\n\n# Expected behaviour\n\nNo change occurs.\n\n# Actual behaviour\n\nThe value is set to false, regardless of its previous state.",
